WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.240 --> 00:00:02.720
The year was 1861.

00:00:02.720 --> 00:00:08.080
Arthur Du Plessis, one of the world’s most
renowned explorers and adventurers, hacked

00:00:08.080 --> 00:00:12.560
through the thick vines of the Amazon Rainforest
with a well-worn machete.

00:00:12.560 --> 00:00:17.360
He grunted and strained, his clothes heavy
and skin slick with sweat.

00:00:17.360 --> 00:00:21.600
He took a deep swig from his canteen and paused
briefly to breathe.

00:00:21.600 --> 00:00:27.040
This was the second week of his solo expedition
into the Lung of the World, and the process

00:00:27.040 --> 00:00:28.480
had been grueling.

00:00:28.480 --> 00:00:33.360
He’d fought off piranhas, electric eels,
and invasive candiru fish while wading and

00:00:33.360 --> 00:00:35.680
kayaking down the Amazon River.

00:00:35.680 --> 00:00:40.880
He’d contended with tribesmen and poachers,
and narrowly dodged his fair share of poisonous

00:00:40.880 --> 00:00:44.640
beasties that could take down prey three times
their size.

00:00:44.640 --> 00:00:50.240
No sane man would brave this horror for its
own sake, but Arthur had as good a reason

00:00:50.240 --> 00:00:56.560
as any: He was searching for his younger brother,
Joseph Du Plessis, who had disappeared a month

00:00:56.560 --> 00:00:58.800
earlier during a trek through the Amazon.

00:00:58.800 --> 00:01:03.840
Joseph had always admired his brother’s
wild adventures, and sought to imitate him.

00:01:03.840 --> 00:01:08.160
It was for that very reason that Arthur had
felt responsible for his brother’s current

00:01:08.160 --> 00:01:11.440
predicament, and made it his mission to rescue
him.

00:01:11.440 --> 00:01:14.720
The Amazon is an ancient and cruel mistress.

00:01:14.720 --> 00:01:19.920
The arrogant and foolish have hoped to conquer
or tame her for centuries, but countless men

00:01:19.920 --> 00:01:23.520
had disappeared in the pulsing heart of this
green behemoth.

00:01:23.520 --> 00:01:28.320
Arthur may have been a world-class explorer,
in a different league to many of the others

00:01:28.320 --> 00:01:33.440
whose lives this green inferno had handily
taken, but there were creatures lurking deep

00:01:33.440 --> 00:01:36.880
in the Amazon that went beyond even Arthur’s
knowledge.

00:01:36.880 --> 00:01:42.080
The kind of beasts that would make the darkest
and most twisted nightmares look comparatively

00:01:42.080 --> 00:01:43.200
inviting.

00:01:43.200 --> 00:01:46.640
Beasts like SCP-2031.

00:01:46.640 --> 00:01:51.520
If Joseph was able to send Arthur one more
message before it all came to a horrible end,

00:01:51.520 --> 00:01:55.040
we could only imagine it’d be something
like “Don’t come looking for me.

00:01:55.040 --> 00:01:56.400
It’s already too late.

00:01:56.400 --> 00:01:58.480
But there’s still time to save yourself,
brother.

00:01:58.480 --> 00:02:00.640
Stay away, for god’s sake, stay away.

00:02:01.280 --> 00:02:03.280
You have no idea what you’re dealing with
here.

00:02:04.000 --> 00:02:04.880
Forget about me.

00:02:05.520 --> 00:02:07.520
Go while there’s still time.”

00:02:07.520 --> 00:02:12.400
Sadly for Arthur Du Plessis, that time was
about to run out.

00:02:12.400 --> 00:02:16.480
He ventured further into the depths of the
Amazon, where even light was scarce under

00:02:16.480 --> 00:02:18.240
the thick canopy above.

00:02:18.240 --> 00:02:23.280
A mighty green Anaconda slithered through
a nearby tributary, tongue flailing in search

00:02:23.280 --> 00:02:24.160
of prey.

00:02:24.160 --> 00:02:29.600
An Amazonian giant centipede - a centipede
so large and vicious it preys on snakes and

00:02:29.600 --> 00:02:33.360
bats - skittered up a nearby&nbsp;
tree on 46 needle-like&nbsp;

00:02:33.360 --> 00:02:34.240
legs.

00:02:34.240 --> 00:02:39.680
A big, meaty tarantula deftly navigated the
branches above, while tree frogs with poison

00:02:39.680 --> 00:02:44.880
potent enough to put an entire army six feet
under hopped through the rich undergrowth.

00:02:44.880 --> 00:02:47.120
Humans held no power here.

00:02:47.120 --> 00:02:49.920
Arthur fell to his knees and began to weep.

00:02:49.920 --> 00:02:54.640
His foolish ambitions had gotten his dear
brother killed in this awful place.

00:02:54.640 --> 00:03:00.320
Shot to death by poachers, strangled by anacondas,
or eaten alive by vicious bull sharks in the

00:03:00.320 --> 00:03:01.360
Amazon river.

00:03:01.360 --> 00:03:06.480
There were so many horrible ways that Joseph
could have died, and in the absence of ever

00:03:06.480 --> 00:03:10.720
finding a body, all of them would simultaneously
be true.

00:03:10.720 --> 00:03:13.920
The Du Plessis family would never know peace.

00:03:13.920 --> 00:03:18.800
There would be a void, an emptiness, in all
of their hearts forever.

00:03:18.800 --> 00:03:23.600
But just when Arthur was about to give up
hope, something miraculous happened: He saw

00:03:23.600 --> 00:03:27.040
a human figure, stumbling around faintly in
the distance.

00:03:27.040 --> 00:03:32.080
Arthur drew his trusty pistol, assuming it
could be a poacher or a hostile tribesman,

00:03:32.080 --> 00:03:34.160
but something was different.

00:03:34.160 --> 00:03:39.040
The figure had its back to Arthur, but he
recognized its shirt - a distinctive shade

00:03:39.040 --> 00:03:40.320
of light blue.

00:03:40.320 --> 00:03:44.560
Just like the shirt that Arthur had bought
for Joseph on his previous birthday.

00:03:44.560 --> 00:03:45.440
Could it be?

00:03:45.440 --> 00:03:46.960
Was this really him?

00:03:46.960 --> 00:03:49.440
Arthur holstered his weapon and jumped to
his feet.

00:03:49.440 --> 00:03:53.280
He couldn’t let this figure get away, even
if there was only the tiniest chance it could

00:03:53.280 --> 00:03:56.800
actually be his brother and not some kind
of forest mirage.

00:03:56.800 --> 00:04:01.680
Arthur ran towards the figure with the last
of his energy reserves, panting and wheezing.

00:04:01.680 --> 00:04:06.560
He called his brother’s name again and again,
but the figure didn’t respond.

00:04:06.560 --> 00:04:09.200
It just stumbled along, as though drunk.

00:04:09.200 --> 00:04:14.800
But the closer Arthur got, the more certain
he was that this was indeed his brother.

00:04:14.800 --> 00:04:18.800
The height, the hair, the clothes, the build.

00:04:18.800 --> 00:04:22.960
It was Joseph Du Plessis, but why wasn’t
he responding?

00:04:22.960 --> 00:04:25.040
Why wouldn’t he turn around?

00:04:25.040 --> 00:04:28.240
As Arthur finally reached the figure, he ground
to a halt.

00:04:28.240 --> 00:04:32.960
The most profound sense of dread fell over
him like a sudden monsoon.

00:04:32.960 --> 00:04:38.800
Something unnatural, something truly terrible,
was about to happen, but he didn’t know

00:04:38.800 --> 00:04:43.440
what - and moreover, it was too late to stop
now.

00:04:43.440 --> 00:04:47.520
Feeling anxiety prickling up his legs and
back, Arthur reached forward to grab his brother

00:04:47.520 --> 00:04:49.680
by the shoulder, the word “Joseph?”

00:04:49.680 --> 00:04:51.200
trembling on his lips.

00:04:51.200 --> 00:04:55.680
When Arthur’s hand touched Joseph’s shoulder,
he felt a fear greater than anything he’d

00:04:55.680 --> 00:04:57.360
experienced before.

00:04:57.360 --> 00:05:01.280
Something was moving beneath the skin of Joseph’s
shoulder.

00:05:01.280 --> 00:05:07.840
Something writhing and alive, a million tiny
creatures all working together in his brother’s

00:05:07.840 --> 00:05:08.560
flesh.

00:05:08.560 --> 00:05:12.240
Before he could even draw his hand away, his
brother turned.

00:05:12.240 --> 00:05:16.560
Or rather, the creatures that were wearing
his brother’s body turned around.

00:05:16.560 --> 00:05:20.160
Arthur couldn’t help but scream at the horrible
sight before him.

00:05:20.160 --> 00:05:25.600
His brother’s face looked loose and rotten,
aging skin hanging off of a rotten skull.

00:05:25.600 --> 00:05:29.200
His jaw hung loose, no tongue inside.

00:05:29.200 --> 00:05:31.040
No eyes, either.

00:05:31.040 --> 00:05:36.720
Just millions of ants swarming in and out
of Joseph Du Plessis’ vacant, dead face.

00:05:36.720 --> 00:05:40.960
The ants were huge and spiny, with long, curved
mandibles.

00:05:40.960 --> 00:05:46.640
Eciton burchellii, a particularly hardy species
of New World Army Ant.

00:05:46.640 --> 00:05:50.400
Arthur stepped back, babbling in terror at
what became of his brother.

00:05:50.400 --> 00:05:55.200
The Joseph-suit stepped forward towards him,
and almost instinctively, Arthur pushed him

00:05:55.200 --> 00:06:00.480
with both hands, feeling the nightmarish activity
swarming beneath the loose cover of Joseph’s

00:06:00.480 --> 00:06:01.680
bony chest.

00:06:01.680 --> 00:06:05.360
The Joseph-suit tumbled backward, tripping
over a rock, and burst.

00:06:05.360 --> 00:06:10.560
There were no organs left inside his brother
now, they’d been eaten long ago.

00:06:10.560 --> 00:06:16.960
It was just a thin tarpaulin of grey skin
over dry bones, and of course, millions upon

00:06:16.960 --> 00:06:22.160
millions of ants, now making a beeline for
Arthur with the frightening military precision

00:06:22.160 --> 00:06:25.200
any naturalist could expect&nbsp;
from Eciton burchellii.

00:06:25.200 --> 00:06:29.760
But while army ants could be a formidable
and frightening foe in their own right, nobody

00:06:29.760 --> 00:06:32.480
had seen any ants like this before.

00:06:32.480 --> 00:06:35.840
Well, nobody who’d lived to tell the tale,
at least.

00:06:35.840 --> 00:06:39.600
Arthur turned to flee, but sadly, it was already
too late for him.

00:06:39.600 --> 00:06:44.080
What he thought were mere prickles of anxiety
were actually an invasion force of Eciton

00:06:44.080 --> 00:06:48.560
burchellii soldiers, which had positioned
themselves over key nerves and ligaments on

00:06:48.560 --> 00:06:50.400
his legs and spine.

00:06:50.400 --> 00:06:55.440
As Arthur tried to run away, the ants began
to bite into him, cutting through skin, rending

00:06:55.440 --> 00:06:59.280
bone, and munching into the chewy neurons
underneath.

00:06:59.280 --> 00:07:04.400
Arthur felt intense flashes of pain all over
his body, before collapsing to the ground,

00:07:04.400 --> 00:07:05.600
paralyzed.

00:07:05.600 --> 00:07:08.480
That’s when the true horrors began.

00:07:08.480 --> 00:07:13.280
If there was one consolation for Arthur in
the last terrible hours of his life, he would

00:07:13.280 --> 00:07:17.360
at least know, first hand, exactly how his
brother died.

00:07:17.360 --> 00:07:21.200
He couldn’t move, but he could feel everything.

00:07:21.200 --> 00:07:24.960
The creatures chewed through the flesh of
his extremities, cutting holes in his skin

00:07:24.960 --> 00:07:28.880
and creating openings for swarms of their
insect brethren to enter through.

00:07:28.880 --> 00:07:34.560
Arthur felt like he was on fire as the swarm
entered his body, but was unable to do anything

00:07:34.560 --> 00:07:35.440
about it.

00:07:35.440 --> 00:07:39.440
Death by these creatures is a slow and torturous
experience.

00:07:39.440 --> 00:07:43.760
Unlike their non-anomalous counterparts, the
swarms don’t immediately start devouring

00:07:43.760 --> 00:07:45.600
all available soft tissue.

00:07:45.600 --> 00:07:51.040
SCP-2031 want to keep their prey alive while
they renovate their new home.

00:07:51.040 --> 00:07:55.520
Arthur finally died two days later - from
dehydration.

00:07:55.520 --> 00:08:00.240
It was at this point that the creatures finally
began eating his organs and evenly distributing

00:08:00.240 --> 00:08:02.160
their colony throughout his body.

00:08:02.160 --> 00:08:07.680
The ants even produce an enzyme that slows
the decaying process for their deceased hosts.

00:08:07.680 --> 00:08:12.000
That’s why Joseph Du Plessis didn’t look
a whole lot worse by the time Arthur found

00:08:12.000 --> 00:08:16.320
him, even though he’d already suffered a
month of post-mortem infestation.

00:08:16.320 --> 00:08:20.640
Not long after Arthur’s death, the Arthur-suit
got up and walked away.

00:08:20.640 --> 00:08:25.440
The world would never know how or why Arthur
Du Plessis and his brother disappeared in

00:08:25.440 --> 00:08:31.760
the dark heart of the Amazon jungle, but perhaps
for the sake of those who loved them, ignorance

00:08:31.760 --> 00:08:34.560
is actually kinder than the truth.

00:08:34.560 --> 00:08:39.600
It would be almost a century before the Foundation
finally discovered these creatures on a nearby

00:08:39.600 --> 00:08:45.600
farm, designated them SCP-2031, and began
containment and testing.

00:08:45.600 --> 00:08:50.240
They soon became aware of what Arthur, Joseph,
and many others had learned the hard way:

00:08:50.240 --> 00:08:53.280
While they may be relatively&nbsp;
ineffectual individually,&nbsp;

00:08:53.280 --> 00:08:55.600
together, these insects were a real force

00:08:55.600 --> 00:08:56.880
to be reckoned with.

00:08:56.880 --> 00:09:01.360
Very few non-anomalous animals had any chance
of escaping them once they’d set their sights

00:09:01.360 --> 00:09:04.560
on a target and begun assuming their attack
positions.

00:09:04.560 --> 00:09:11.280
In one observed instance, SCP-2031 soldiers
were able to take down a 1000kg Angus Bull

00:09:11.280 --> 00:09:16.320
in five minutes, most of which was just spent
getting their soldiers into their proper positions

00:09:16.320 --> 00:09:18.400
over the spine and leg ligaments.

00:09:18.400 --> 00:09:22.640
The Foundation just got extremely lucky that
these vicious insect predators happened to

00:09:22.640 --> 00:09:24.960
be isolated to some pretty specific areas&nbsp;

00:09:24.960 --> 00:09:28.080
in South America, thanks&nbsp;
to the climate requirements

00:09:28.080 --> 00:09:29.680
of their habitats.

00:09:29.680 --> 00:09:34.720
In fact, pretty much all of the specimens
the Foundation found were all in one place.

00:09:34.720 --> 00:09:41.520
The creatures had developed a particularly
frightening form of Ant Farm known as SCP-2031-A:

00:09:41.520 --> 00:09:46.160
An isolated containment zone on a stretch
of farmland where the ants could find hosts

00:09:46.160 --> 00:09:50.960
in the form of live people and animals, keeping
them relatively isolated.

00:09:50.960 --> 00:09:58.000
Twenty-seven separate SCP-2031 colonies were
first found on this farm, inhabiting and operating

00:09:58.000 --> 00:10:00.080
twenty-seven different corpses.

00:10:00.080 --> 00:10:02.320
These included fifteen cows.

00:10:02.320 --> 00:10:03.840
Five different horses.

00:10:03.840 --> 00:10:05.520
Three domestic pigs.

00:10:05.520 --> 00:10:06.480
One dog.

00:10:06.480 --> 00:10:10.720
And most fascinating of&nbsp;
all, three human specimens:&nbsp;

00:10:10.720 --> 00:10:14.160
An adult male, an adult female, and a child

00:10:14.160 --> 00:10:16.080
of unspecified gender.

00:10:16.080 --> 00:10:20.560
What’s even more fascinating than the efficacy
of these ants in attacking all different kinds

00:10:20.560 --> 00:10:25.280
of prey is their deftness at mimicking the
behavior of their hosts.

00:10:25.280 --> 00:10:29.920
This isn’t a Reconstructive Maggots situation
- see our video on that nightmare for further

00:10:29.920 --> 00:10:34.240
information - the ants attempt to make their
hosts actually act like the creatures they

00:10:34.240 --> 00:10:35.280
once were.

00:10:35.280 --> 00:10:39.520
The Foundation were astonished to see that
the three human-suits seemed to actually go

00:10:39.520 --> 00:10:45.120
through the motions of running the farm - watering
the “livestock,” dispensing feed, moving

00:10:45.120 --> 00:10:48.960
other SCP-2031 colonies from one pasture to
another.

00:10:48.960 --> 00:10:54.240
The human child-suit would even spend extensive
time playing with the dog-suit, engaging in

00:10:54.240 --> 00:10:56.960
games such as fetch or mock wrestling.

00:10:56.960 --> 00:11:03.200
How the SCP-2031 colonies are able to do this
is unknown - working theories include rigorous

00:11:03.200 --> 00:11:08.240
observation of their targets before colonization,
and the colony hive mind somehow picking up

00:11:08.240 --> 00:11:11.520
residual thoughts or muscle memory from their
victims.

00:11:11.520 --> 00:11:17.760
Non-anomalous ants introduced to the SCP-2031
colonies also begin exhibiting anomalous traits,

00:11:17.760 --> 00:11:20.800
so the effects may somehow be contagious.

00:11:20.800 --> 00:11:24.480
One of the most fascinating moments of all
came when the structural integrity of the

00:11:24.480 --> 00:11:29.600
dog-suit finally gave out, leading to its
colony exiting the body and returning to more

00:11:29.600 --> 00:11:33.760
nomadic behavior typical of army ants in search
of a new host.

00:11:33.760 --> 00:11:38.080
The strange part was that the human-suits
actually seemed to grieve for the deceased

00:11:38.080 --> 00:11:42.720
dog-suit, with the child-suit becoming somewhat
distressed that their playmate was suddenly

00:11:42.720 --> 00:11:43.440
gone.

00:11:43.440 --> 00:11:48.800
The two adult human-suits even took the carcass
of the dog-suit and buried it in another pasture.

00:11:48.800 --> 00:11:54.240
It was unlike anything the Foundation had
observed with SCP-2031 before.

00:11:54.240 --> 00:11:58.000
At what point did mimicry become sincere behavior?

00:11:58.000 --> 00:12:02.480
Because now, SCP-2031 was seriously blurring
the lines.

00:12:02.480 --> 00:12:07.360
It is in the best interest of the Foundation
to keep this little ant farm going, both to

00:12:07.360 --> 00:12:12.960
keep SCP-2031 distracted from venturing further
and causing trouble, and to further study

00:12:12.960 --> 00:12:19.440
the fascinating behaviors and dynamics exhibited
by SCP-2031 colonies in captivity.

00:12:19.440 --> 00:12:24.480
One of the researchers has already put in
a request for a new golden retriever.

00:12:24.480 --> 00:12:30.680
Now go check out “SCP-2852 Sadistic Madman
Party Crasher | Cousin Johnny” and “SCP-5049

00:12:30.680 --> 00:12:36.560
- The Skin Salesman - Demon Dan's Discount
Homunculus Depot” for more SCPs that’ll

00:12:36.560 --> 00:12:39.040
give you utterly horrific fates!

